menu "Desk Buddy appearance"

    choice BUDDY_THEME
        prompt "Screen theme"
        default BUDDY_THEME_PAPER
        help
            The colours the face and its widgets are drawn with.
            Paper is warm off-white for daytime. Ember is warm near-black
            with a brighter face, for a desk at night. Palettes and their
            contrast checks are in main/face/face_theme.h and docs/DESIGN.md.

        config BUDDY_THEME_PAPER
            bool "Paper (day)"
        config BUDDY_THEME_EMBER
            bool "Ember (night)"
    endchoice

    config BUDDY_UI_REDUCED_MOTION
        bool "Reduce interface motion"
        default n
        help
            Captions appear and disappear without sliding or fading.
            The face itself still blinks and changes expression.

    config BUDDY_UI_STATUS_CHIP
        bool "Show the status chip (clock, listening meter, online, mic off)"
        default y
        help
            A small chip in the top-left corner that reports what the box is
            really doing: the microphone switch is off, it is listening (with
            a live level meter), a request to the home or cloud brain is out,
            or, when nothing is happening, the time once the clock has synced
            over Wi-Fi. With this off, mute is still shown on the face.

    config BUDDY_UI_STATUS_CLOCK
        bool "Show the time in the status chip when idle"
        default y
        depends on BUDDY_UI_STATUS_CHIP
        help
            Only shown once the clock has synced (net_time). Before that the
            chip stays hidden rather than showing a wrong time.

endmenu
